# Censprobe Docker build context exclusions
#
# Without this, every COPY of packages/<name> drags in the developer's
# local virtualenv (~38MB), pytest/hypothesis caches, build artifacts,
# and reports/ data. Layer sizes balloon and CI cache hits get rarer
# (any change to .venv invalidates the COPY layer).
#
# Each per-image Dockerfile uses ``COPY packages/<name>`` — the patterns
# below apply uniformly to every build.

# ── Python build / venv artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.venv
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/coverage.xml
**/junit.xml
**/htmlcov
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info

# ── Reports + logs (operator-side data, never relevant to image build) ───────
reports/
logs.txt

# ── Editor / VCS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*~

# ── Tooling configs not consumed by Docker build ─────────────────────────────
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.gitleaks.toml
.yamllint.yaml
.hadolint.yaml
.sonarcloud.properties
sonar-project.properties

# ── Docs (not needed at runtime) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
*.md

# ── Tests trees (not needed at runtime; keep source-only inside images) ──────
**/tests/
tests/
